          "messageID": "msg_002",
          "type": "step-start"
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_002b",
          "sessionID": "ses_26",
          "messageID": "msg_002",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "git doesn't delete uncommitted work just because you switch branches. If your changes would conflict with the branch you're switching to, checkout actually refuses and tells you 'your local changes would be overwritten' - it won't silently blow them away. If there's no conflict, your edits just carry over to the new branch. What probably happened last week was something else, like a hard reset, a stash that never got popped, or a file that just doesn't exist on the other branch."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_002c",
          "sessionID": "ses_26",
          "messageID": "msg_002",
          "type": "step-finish",
          "reason": "stop",
          "cost": 0.01,
