          "id": "prt_004b",
          "sessionID": "ses_26",
          "messageID": "msg_004",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What commands exactly do you run when that happens - just `git checkout main`, or something else first? Checkout alone, with changes that would conflict, is blocked by git rather than silently deleting anything. Work that seems to 'disappear' is almost always one of: the file you edited doesn't exist on main (so it looks gone, but it's still there when you switch back), a `git clean` or `git reset --hard` ran somewhere, or changes went into a stash you forgot about."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_004c",
          "sessionID": "ses_26",
          "messageID": "msg_004",
